#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""offload: run heavy work on short-lived Hetzner Cloud servers so the Mac stays usable.

https://github.com/pipamann/offload-to-hetzner (MIT). Uses `hcloud` with a Hetzner Cloud API token (read & write):
$HCLOUD_TOKEN, or the variable named in $OFFLOAD_TOKEN_VAR, looked up in the environment, then in the files listed in
$OFFLOAD_SECRET_FILES, then in hcloud's active context. The token travels only as an environment variable, never on
a command line. Every server gets its own SSH key, labels for owner, task, run and expiry, and a watchdog on this Mac
that deletes server and key at the expiry time, also right after the Mac wakes up. A launchd job (the sweeper) covers
reboots and crashes.

  offload types [--location fsn1]                       live prices of the server types on sale
  offload create <task> [--type cx53] [--location fsn1] [--ttl 4h] [--from <base>] [--setup docker|<file>]
  offload push <task> [<local-dir>] [<remote-dir>]      git-tracked + untracked files; keeps node_modules/.venv remotely
  offload put <task> <local-path> <remote-path>         one file, or a folder's contents
  offload exec <task> [--cwd <dir>] -- '<command>'      runs now, exits with the remote exit status
  offload exec <task> --detach <job> [--cwd <dir>] -- '<command>'   keeps running when SSH drops or the Mac sleeps
  offload wait <task> <job> [--timeout 3h]              waits for a detached job, exits with its status
  offload logs <task> <job> [-n 40] [-f]
  offload get <task> <remote-path> <local-path>
  offload ls                                            all offload servers in the project, with cost so far
  offload rm <task>...                                  deletes server and key, checks both are gone, stops the watchdog
  offload clean [--mine | --owner <owner> | --all]      default: only expired servers, orphaned keys and local state
  offload sweeper install|uninstall|status              launchd job: `offload sweep` at login and every 15 minutes
  offload base create <base> [--setup docker|<file>]    snapshot to start servers from; billed while it exists
  offload base ls | offload base rm <base>
"""
